# CHERQAiN — optional online-provider API keys.
#
# CHERQAiN runs fully offline with Ollama / LM Studio and needs NONE of these.
# They are only required if you route CHAT through an online provider (OpenAI,
# Anthropic, Google Gemini, DeepSeek, Z.AI, or OpenRouter). Embeddings,
# indexing, and retrieval always stay
# local, so your notes never leave the machine in bulk even with a key set.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   Dev (running `python launch.py` from a terminal): copy this file to the repo
#   root as `.env`, or just export the vars in your shell profile.
#
#   Packaged .app: a Finder-launched bundle does NOT inherit your shell
#   environment, so keys in ~/.zshrc are invisible to it. Copy this file to:
#       ~/Library/Application Support/ChatEKLD/.env
#   then uncomment and fill in the key(s) you use. A real shell variable always
#   wins over this file (launch.py loads it with override=False).
#
# Keys are read from the environment at call time and are NEVER written to
# config.json or returned by the API.

# --- Storage & Data Directory Overrides (optional) ---
# By default, CHERQAiN stores config.json, SQLite databases, logs, and local
# RAG indexes under ~/Library/Application Support/ChatEKLD on macOS (or
# ~/.local/share/ChatEKLD on Linux). Uncomment to relocate the entire data
# directory or individual storage paths:
# CHERQAIN_BASE_DIR=/path/to/custom/cherqain_data
# CHERQAIN_DB_PATH=/path/to/custom/uploads.db
# CHERQAIN_INDEX_DIR=/path/to/custom/obsidian_storage
# CHERQAIN_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/custom/obsidian_cache

# --- Online LLM Provider Keys (optional) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
# ZAI_API_KEY=...            # Z.AI / Zhipu GLM (ZHIPU_API_KEY also accepted)
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...   # OpenRouter (aggregator; namespaced model ids)

# Agent web search (NOT an LLM key). The vault agent's optional web_search
# tool is Tavily-backed and triple-gated: the Settings toggle must be on, the
# active chat provider must be ONLINE, and this key must be in the environment
# at call time. Without it the toggle simply reports web search unavailable.
# Same discipline: never written to config.json, never returned by the API.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...

# Biblio Tagging → Zotero (NOT an LLM key). Zotero's LOCAL API is read-only
# before Zotero 10, so writing tags to your Zotero library needs a zotero.org
# Web API key with write permission (Settings → Feeds/API on zotero.org).
# Same discipline: read at call time, never written to config.json.
# ZOTERO_API_KEY=...
